{
  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: image_only, resnet50, avgpool → acc 0.328), the most fundamental uncertainty is whether adding the RNA modality provides meaningful signal beyond the image alone. config_008 (multimodal, scgpt, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) keeps the image encoder and aggregation identical to config_001, so any performance difference can be attributed primarily to the addition of RNA via scgpt and the weighted fusion. This directly tests the core hypothesis of the multimodal profiling study. scgpt is a well-established pretrained single-cell RNA encoder, making it a principled first choice for the RNA modality. Establishing whether RNA adds value is the highest-priority design question before investing budget in encoder variants, aggregation strategies, or fusion alternatives. If config_008 substantially outperforms config_001, we can then exploit by testing better encoders/aggregation; if it does not, we learn that the bottleneck lies elsewhere (e.g., image representation or profile setting) and redirect exploration accordingly."
}

